! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F204A sub-test 5
! (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf p.53, octal 012355.00-012362.40) --
! a DISCRIMINATING M+ (Add to Memory) test. Unlike F204A1-3 (which check
! that far-apart exponents drop the low operand, and so pass even for a
! no-op M+), F204A5 uses NORMAL-range operands and checks the SUM
! against a precomputed expected result -- so a wrong M+ fails it.
!
!   L(BU),FPK35 / ST(BU,64),ROS   ROS := FPK35 (N range)
!   L(U),FPK39 / M+(U),ROS         ROS := FPK35 + FPK39 (both N range)
!   L(BU,64),FPK32                 acc := FPK32, the EXPECTED sum
!                                  (listing: "check result exp++2 and
!                                   fract+1")
!   CT0110(BU,64),ROS              connect acc (FPK32) with ROS (sum);
!                                  RGZ comes on iff they DIFFER
!   SIC,SEN / BRGZ,SERS            error (RGZ on) if sum != FPK32
! So the model reaches PASS iff M+ computed FPK35+FPK39 == FPK32; a
! wrong sum branches to the SERS FAIL halt. Because the operands are
! N range (not flagged), M+ goes through fpAdd's normal fraction-shift
! path -- the path a fraction-alignment injection actually exercises,
! which makes this a real discriminating test (F204A1-3 were not).
!
! Substitutions (SSIP framework, real listed addresses): SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch, PASS (octal 12363,
! F204A6's start) -> halt. ROS (octal 22355) is the memory operand.
! Constants FPK32/FPK35/FPK39 from the pool p.176.
!
! Instructions: L(BU)/ST(BU,64) (VFL), L(U)/M+(U) (FP), L(BU,64), CT0110
! (connective), SIC, BRGZ -- all implemented; encodings checked against
! the page. verify_fp_arith_f204a5_listing.py checks bit-for-bit.
!
! Observed: the model halts at PASS -- M+ computes FPK35+FPK39 == FPK32,
! matching the diagnostic's expected result. Discriminating injection
! (fpAdd's same-sign fraction add made to drop the added operand,
! `sum = fb + fs` -> `sum = fb`): halts at SERS, exactly as predicted,
! since the M+ result then differs from FPK32. Reversed by the exact
! inverse edit (AGENTS.md rule 2). NOTE: an exponent-alignment injection
! (`>> adiff` -> `>> 0`) does NOT discriminate here, because FPK35 and
! FPK39 share an exponent (adiff = 0); that is why F204A1-3 (far-apart
! exponents, "error if fractions added") also cannot catch a broken M+
! and this sub-test, which checks the sum against a precomputed result,
! is the one that can.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0
        SLC, (8)22355.0
ROS     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool p.176) --
        SLC, (8)22045.0
FPK32   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001177777777777777760
        SLC, (8)22050.0
FPK35   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001125252525252525240
        SLC, (8)22054.0
FPK39   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0001052525252525252520

! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)12355.0
F204A5  L(BU), FPK35        ! EXP IN N RANGE
        ST(BU,64), ROS
        L(U), FPK39         ! EXP N RANGE
        M+(U), ROS
        L(BU,64), FPK32     ! the expected result
        CT0110(BU,64), ROS
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS          ! error if sum != FPK32

! -- PASS halt where F204A6 begins --
        SLC, (8)12363.0
PASS    BEW, $

        END, F204A5
